Disney today increased the prices on several of its Disney+ and Hulu streaming plans, with the increase coming exactly one year after <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2025/09/23/disney-plus-price-increase-2025/">Disney's last price hike</a>.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2023/09/disney.jpg" alt="" width="2500" height="1406" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-909605" /><br/>
Premium ad-free plans are &#36;2 to &#36;2.50 more expensive per month, while Disney's ad-supported Disney+ and Hulu plans are &#36;0.50 higher per month. The ad-supported Disney+ and Hulu bundle has not changed in price, and that's what Disney is steering customers toward.<br/>
<ul><br/>
 	<li><strong>Disney+ (Ads)</strong> - &#36;12.49, up from &#36;11.99</li><br/>
 	<li><strong>Disney+ (No Ads)</strong> - &#36;21.49, up from &#36;18.99</li><br/>
 	<li><strong>Hulu (Ads)</strong> - &#36;12.49, up from &#36;11.99</li><br/>
 	<li><strong>Hulu (No Ads)</strong> - &#36;21.49, up from &#36;18.99</li><br/>
 	<li><strong>Disney+, Hulu Bundle (Ads)</strong> - &#36;12.99, no change</li><br/>
 	<li><strong>Disney+, Hulu Bundle (No Ads)</strong> - &#36;21.99, up from &#36;19.99</li><br/>
 	<li><strong>Disney+, ESPN, Hulu Bundle (Ads)</strong> - &#36;21.99, up from &#36;19.99</li><br/>
 	<li><strong>Disney+ (No Ads), Hulu (No Ads), ESPN Select (Ads)</strong> - &#36;32.99, up from &#36;29.99</li><br/>
 	<li><strong>Disney+, Hulu, HBO Max Basic (Ads)</strong> - &#36;21.99, up from &#36;19.99</li><br/>
 	<li><strong>Disney+, Hulu, HBO Max Basic (No Ads)</strong> - &#36;34.99, up from &#36;32.99</li><br/>
</ul><br/>
Bundles with ESPN or HBO Max are also &#36;2 to &#36;3 more expensive. Buying a standalone Disney+ or Hulu plan is just &#36;0.50 cheaper per month than getting a bundle, both with ads and without. Disney is pushing bundles because it has been merging Hulu content into the Disney+ app to create an all-in-one experience.<br/>
<br/>
When Disney+ launched <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2019/11/12/disney-plus-now-available/">in November 2019</a>, it was priced at &#36;6.99 per month. It did not have ads at the time, with Disney introducing its first ad-supported plan in 2022. Pricing for the no-ad option has increased more than 200% in nearly seven years.<br/>
<br/>
Apple's <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2019/11/01/apple-tv-plus-launch/">streaming TV service launched</a> right around the same time as Disney+ for &#36;4.99 per month. Today, the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/apple-tv/">Apple TV</a> service is &#36;14.99 per month, also a 200% increase. Other streaming services like Netflix and HBO Max raise prices regularly too.<br/>
<br/>
